  "descriptions": [
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs",
      "text": "BPool single-sided join/exit math with SideStaking gulp accounting. Lost: 127.86K mOCEAN"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "Ocean Protocol's BPool/SideStaking pools on Polygon were exploited on June 25, 2026, using a logic flaw in single-sided join/exit accounting. The attacker drained about 127,861 mOCEAN, valued at roughly $11.8K, by repeatedly minting and burning pool shares across multiple Ocean pools, extracting more mOCEAN than contributed. A broken accounting invariant in Ocean Protocol's BPool implementation allowed a single-sided join followed by a single-sided exit to mint and redeem pool shares at mismatched rates, amplified by SideStaking's automatic datatoken co-staking. The attacker could repeatedly increase their base-token balance through this sequence."
    }
  ],
